,"followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiena/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiena/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiena/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiena/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiena/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiena/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiena/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiena/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiena/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-02T05:19:34Z","updated_at":"2025-06-15T07:08:16Z","body":"Ready for review.\r\nThe demo site requires Chrome 137+ due to its use of JSPI.\r\nI wanted to use `ASYNCIFY=1` in SCsub but ran into errors, so I'm currently using `ASYNCIFY=2` for JSPI.\r\n\r\nDemo site: https://shiena.github.io/godot-camerafeed-demo/\r\nDemo source code: https://github.com/shiena/godot-camerafeed-demo","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2928819700/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2929726385","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106784#issuecomment-2929726385","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106784","id":2929726385,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6uoBOx","user":{"login":"shiena","id":1295639,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyOTU2Mzk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1295639?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiena","html_url":"https://github.com/shiena","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiena/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiena/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiena/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiena/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiena/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiena/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiena/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiena/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiena/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-02T09:44:09Z","updated_at":"2025-06-02T09:44:09Z","body":"> That said, it should be possible to implement the API by relying on callbacks instead of requiring asyncify.\r\n\r\nI'm trying to get a list of `CameraFeed` objects using `CameraServer.feeds()` after setting `CameraServer.monitoring_feeds = true` in GDScript. Once I have a `CameraFeed`, I then want to retrieve its available formats using `CameraFeed.formats`.\r\n\r\nHowever, both of these methods return a JavaScript Promise, which makes using callbacks inherently slow.\r\nIf there's an alternative approach, I'd be happy to try it out immediately.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2929726385/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2940943589","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106784#issuecomment-2940943589","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106784","id":2940943589,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6vSzzl","user":{"login":"shiena","id":1295639,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyOTU2Mzk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1295639?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiena","html_url":"https://github.com/shiena","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiena/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiena/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiena/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiena/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiena/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiena/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiena/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiena/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiena/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-04T18:12:27Z","updated_at":"2025-06-15T15:10:29Z","body":"@Faless \r\nRemoved Asyncify dependency and confirmed functionality in the following browsers.\r\n- Chrome v137.0.7151.69\r\n- Firefox ESR v128.11.0esr\r\n- Safari v18.5(20621.2.5.11.8)\r\n\r\nHowever, please note the following limitations:\r\n\r\n- Retrieving the list of camera devices with `CameraServer.monitoring_feeds = true` is an asynchronous operation, so it requires a few frames until the state becomes true.\r\n  https://github.com/shiena/godot-camerafeed-demo/blob/main/scripts/Main.gd#L51-L56\r\n- Firefox ESR does not support `MediaStreamTrack.getCapabilities()`, which means `CameraFeed.formats` and related APIs will not function.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2940943589/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3024554448","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106784#issuecomment-3024554448","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106784","id":3024554448,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc